## Marking derived and modified files (GPL-2.0 §2(a))

Any file carrying scapy-derived material opens with a provenance block, before
the code and after any `#!` line, in that file's comment syntax:

    // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
    //
    // Derived from scapy: scapy/layers/<file>.py
    //   scapy <version>, upstream commit <sha>
    //   Copyright (C) Philippe Biondi and the scapy contributors
    //
    // Changed by the wiry authors:
    //   YYYY-MM-DD — what was changed, in one line

A file that is changed again gains another dated line; existing lines are never
rewritten or removed, because the dates are the record §2(a) asks for. A file
with no scapy-derived material carries no such block — absence is a claim that
the file is wiry's own work, so do not add the block decoratively, and do not
omit it from a file that needs it.

`CONTRIBUTING.md` holds the full procedure. The ledger below is the index; the
